{
 "about": "Plato's Chair inside Muse Glimmer 30B: how spread out each concept's drawings are at several stages inside the model, for Muse Image's doodles and for people's drawings (Google Quick, Draw!), where Muse's doodles collapse, and how well Glimmer names them. Derived statistics only. Exploratory: 35 concepts, 12-16 pictures per source, one model. See docs/plato_glimmer.md.",
 "attribution": "Human drawings: Google Quick, Draw! dataset (Google Creative Lab), CC BY 4.0, https://github.com/googlecreativelab/quickdraw-dataset",
 "models": {
  "namer": "Muse Glimmer 30B (Meta, open weights, self-hosted)",
  "doodles": "Muse Image 1.0 (Meta)"
 },
 "definitions": {
  "spread": "mean pairwise cosine distance between a concept's pictures at the answer position, on states centered over all 920 pictures (higher = more varied)",
  "collapse_layer": "the first decoder layer (of 52) from which Muse Image's doodles stay less than 0.5 times as spread out as people's drawings of the same thing, through layer 52; null if that never happens",
  "name_appears_layer": "median first layer where the word lens reads the accepted name (logit lens)",
  "stages": "projector = the picture after the vision adapter; L13...L52 = decoder layers"
 },
